      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are absolutely right to be concerned about a stroke, even without arm numbness, because facial drooping alone is a major red flag that requires immediate hospital evaluation. Please do not wait to see if it gets better; go to the ER now, and while you are on your way, take 325mg of aspirin immediately to help thin your blood and prevent clotting. Do not try to diagnose it yourself at home, because a stroke can happen in seconds and every minute counts.",
